#5000
The Antechamber of Every Flag~
   Every room flag a CircleMUD bitvector_t can hold is set on this room
at once. The field below is 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEF' - bits 0
through 31, which is as wide as an i386 `long` ever was. Anything from
'G' on would be `1 << 32` in an `int`, which is undefined behaviour in
the C loader rather than a bigger number, so this is the widest field
that is hostile instead of simply broken.
   Bits nothing has a name for come back through `flags_raw`, which is
the escape hatch the yaml format has for exactly this.
~
50 abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEF 0
D0
North, to the room whose description is not ASCII.
~
~
0 -1 5001
S
#5001
Caf’ de l’Encodage…~
   This description is CP1252, not UTF-8, and every byte in it that is
not ASCII is one an archived world file really contains: ’ is the
curly apostrophe in data/world/wld/90.wld, “ and ” the curly
quotes, – and — the en and em dashes, … an ellipsis, and é
è ü ñ the accented letters a builder typed on a machine that
was not this one.
   © 2001. ½ a loaf. 30° to starboard.
~
50 0 1
E
caf’ sign~
   The sign says “Café”, in the encoding it was painted in.
~
D0
North, past the café, to the room that ends in silence.
~
~
0 -1 5002
D2
Back to the Antechamber.
~
~
0 -1 5000
S
#5002
The Room That Ends In Silence~
   This description ends with a deliberately blank line before its
closing tilde. fread_string appends CRLF for every line that does not
contain a tilde, so the loaded string ends with two of them, and a
YAML
literal block cannot carry that back: goccy's re-print right-trims
every trailing newline off the node regardless of the chomping
indicator. The yaml writer quotes and escapes it instead.

~
50 0 2
D0
North, to the room with a carriage return in it.
~
~
0 -1 5003
D2
Back to the café.
~
~
0 -1 5001
S
#5003
The Room With A Bare Carriage Return~
   The line after this one ends with a literal CR before its newline.
rawLine strips only the '\n', so the CR survives into the string and
fread_string then appends its own CRLF after it:
   That is a bare carriage return once CRLF pairs are folded to LF, and
a bare CR is unrepresentable in a YAML block scalar at all - the spec
folds CR, CRLF and LF alike on decode. obj/0.obj's bug object in the
real archive has fifteen of them in a row.
~
50 0 0
D0
North, to the room with trailing spaces.
~
~
0 -1 5004
D2
Back to the room that ends in silence.
~
~
0 -1 5002
S
#5004
The Room With Trailing Spaces~
   The final line of this description carries its own tilde, so
fread_string returns without appending CRLF, and it carries trailing
spaces before that tilde. A literal block drops them; the writer
quotes the string instead.   ~
50 0 0
D0
North, to the room with a hash in it.
~
~
0 -1 5005
D2
Back to the room with a carriage return in it.
~
~
0 -1 5003
S
#5005
The Room With A Hash In It~
   The next line begins with a '#'. count_hash_records counts those to
size its arrays, and it counts this one, so the loader allocates room
for a record that is not there:
#5005 is prose, not a record header, whatever the record counter says.
   A lone dollar sign is content too, and so is a hash that is not in
the first column: only a tilde ends a string, and only a hash in
column one starts a record. $
~
50 0 0
D0
North, to the gallery.
~
~
0 -1 5006
D2
Back to the room with trailing spaces.
~
~
0 -1 5004
S
#5006
The Gallery of Indented Art~
   Two hand-drawn signs hang here. One is an extra description on the
room; the other is the description of the exit north. Both begin with
more leading whitespace than a later line carries, which is the shape
that makes a YAML literal block decode back to a different string than
it encoded unless an indentation indicator is emitted - and NestedText
cannot reliably emit one at this depth, so it quotes instead.
~
50 0 0
E
sign painted~
        +----------------+
        |  THIS WAY UP   |
        +----------------+
   and underneath, in a smaller hand, someone has added: 'or not'.
~
D0
        /\
       /  \    a gable, drawn in an exit description, six columns deep
      /____\   in the yaml document that comes out the other side
~
gate grille~
1 5003 5007
D2
Back to the room with a hash in it.
~
~
0 -1 5005
S
#5007
The Room That Looks Like Syntax~
   get_line skips a line whose first byte is '*'; fread_string does
not. So the next line is content, and a loader that used the wrong
primitive would silently lose it:
* this line begins with an asterisk and is part of the description.
   The line after this one opens with the colour markup's own
delimiter, which YAML would otherwise read as a flow mapping:
{{red}}not colour, just two braces{{/}}
~
50 0 0
D0
North, to the last room.
~
~
0 -1 5008
D2
Back to the gallery.
~
~
0 -1 5006
S
#5008
The Empty Room~
~
50 0 0
D2
Back to the room that looks like syntax.
~
~
0 -1 5007
S
$
